{%- comment -%}
  Brand image, above the Alcove (D16). The campaign picture first, then the one piece.

  Type sits below the image, never on it, the same rule as every other plate
  (1-shop/04-site-ia.md, "Information stays below the image at every scale"), so no scrim.
  A separate phone image is optional: without one, the desktop image is cropped to 4:5
  around its focal point, which is set on the image itself in Shopify (Edit image > Focal point).
  Until a picture is chosen, a quiet daylight study holds the space. It has no object in it,
  so it can't be mistaken for a product.

  Layout "Beside the words" (split): on a laptop the headline, text and buttons sit to the left of
  the picture, so the first screen says what the shop is and where to go. It shows the phone image
  (4:3) when there is one, which keeps the whole of a wide arrangement in a squarer frame.
  The first link is a button; the second, a quieter text link.

  "Logo as the heading": the shop's lockup is the h1, and the heading becomes the line under it.
  "Just the heading, on one line" (owner, 2026-11-04: "just make it one line"): no logo, text or
  links, in every language, and the heading set smaller on a phone so it stays on one line. A
  setting, not "the text is empty": a translated page keeps the translation of a cleared field.
  A second link to a page that does not exist yet (the viewing page, before it is made in
  Shopify) goes to the contact page instead, so the button never leads nowhere. The test is on
  the handle: for a missing handle Shopify can still answer pages['x'] with an object.

  Owner, 2026-11-18: only the viewing link under the words, centred (show_link off: a setting rather
  than an empty label, for the same reason as one_line above). The heading and the three lines each
  have a typeface setting (heading_face, text_face; styles at the end of assets/hikari.css). First
  the heading was in Aboreto and the lines in handwriting; the owner then swapped them the same day:
  the heading in handwriting, the lines in Aboreto.

  The opening (shell "intro", owner 2026-11-18: "a 海螺 that is large and minimalist" on the banner):
  the picture starts under a veil the colour of the page, a large shell (snippets/conch) draws itself
  on it and its pearl rolls out and glints; then the veil opens in a circle from the pearl and the
  photograph comes through. The script just below the opening tag runs before the picture is parsed,
  so nothing flashes. It plays once per visit (per tab), never with reduced motion, nor when the page
  opens scrolled down; a click, key, tap or scroll opens it at once, and it opens after 7 seconds
  whatever happens. Without JavaScript there is no veil. The photograph loads and paints underneath
  all along, so the page is no slower; the veil waits for it before opening.

  No photograph (shell "banner", owner 2026-11-18: "i dont want to see this photo, too realistic too
  blurry too ugly"): the large shell is the banner's picture, drawn in a hairline on the page's own
  ground above the words, and nothing is downloaded for it. It draws itself once per visit (per tab,
  the same key as the opening), the pearl rolls out and glints; the words are there from the start,
  so nothing waits on it. Reduced motion, no JavaScript, or a second look in the same tab: drawn
  already. The image settings stay, so a photograph can come back by choosing another shell option.

  Backdrop "bloom" (owner, 2026-11-19, after a video of ours, 0:19-0:23: dappled light, a warm glow,
  then the words): behind the shell and the words, pale flowers on ivory linen (generated, no people,
  no jewellery: tools/banner-source), with the shadows of leaves swaying over it and a warm peach light
  that breathes. Once per visit, with the shell's drawing (.is-drawing), the picture comes up out of
  bright light, the leaf shadows pass across it, the glow blooms, and the words come into focus one
  after another. Reduced motion: all of it still, from the start. With the backdrop the photograph is
  never shown (the flowers are the picture), with or without the shell (owner, 2026-11-19: "get rid of
  the shell": shell none, the words centred on the flowers).

  Backdrop "film" (owner and 刘总, 2026-11-19, second version: "直接拿这个视频来做banner"): the banner is our
  2.8-second film (iPhone 4K HDR, made standard-range with macOS avconvert; tools/banner-source/film2).
  From 2026-11-20 to 2026-11-23 the page laid its own words over a film without them; since 2026-11-23
  (owner: "use everything from the 4k video and add no text to the film") the film is the original
  again, with its own words, and the page adds nothing to it (tools/film-without-words.py and the
  words-free films stay in tools/banner-source/film2 as a way back). Phone: the whole portrait film fills the first screen
  under the header. Laptop: a 16:9 band of it, cropped top and bottom around the words (1920 x 1080). Each
  from Settings > Files (film_video, film_video_phone), played once, muted, and held on its last frame; no
  fade into the page, a clean edge, then the three lines and the viewing link on the page colour. Until it
  plays, its first frame (theme image) shows; with reduced motion or without JavaScript, its last frame
  with the words already there. The words are also the page's h1, for screen readers and search.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign img = section.settings.image
  assign img_m = section.settings.image_mobile
  assign fit = section.settings.height
  assign split = false
  if section.settings.layout == 'split'
    assign split = true
  endif
  assign link2 = section.settings.link2
  if link2 contains '/pages/'
    assign ph = link2 | split: '/pages/' | last | split: '?' | first
    assign pg = pages[ph]
    unless pg.handle == ph and pg.url != blank
      assign link2 = pages.contact.url
    endunless
  endif
  assign line = section.settings.one_line
  assign art = false
  if section.settings.shell == 'banner'
    assign art = true
  endif
  assign bloom = false
  if section.settings.backdrop == 'bloom'
    assign bloom = true
  endif
  assign filmed = false
  if section.settings.backdrop == 'film'
    assign filmed = true
  endif
  case fit
    when 'wide'
      assign ratio = 0.4286
    when 'tall'
      assign ratio = 0.75
    else
      assign ratio = 0.5625
  endcase
-%}
<section class="hero{% if split %} hero--split{% endif %}{% if line %} hero--line{% endif %}{% if art %} hero--art{% endif %}{% if section.settings.backdrop == 'bloom' %} hero--bloom{% endif %}{% if filmed %} hero--film{% endif %}{% if section.settings.heading_face != 'theme' %} hero--h-{{ section.settings.heading_face }}{% endif %}{% if section.settings.text_face != 'theme' %} hero--t-{{ section.settings.text_face }}{% endif %}" id="brand" data-bg="#FAF8F3" data-fg="#1C1B18" style="--sec-bg:#FAF8F3;--sec-fg:#1C1B18;">
  {%- comment -%} The banner's own faces (Aboreto, the handwriting), only when it shows words in them (never over the film). {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless filmed -%}{%- unless request.locale.iso_code == 'ar' or request.locale.iso_code == 'zh-CN' or request.locale.iso_code == 'ja' -%}
  {%- if section.settings.heading_face != 'theme' or section.settings.text_face != 'theme' -%}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Aboreto&family=Nothing+You+Could+Do&display=swap">
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- endunless -%}{%- endunless -%}
  {%- if section.settings.shell == 'intro' -%}
  <script>
    (function (s) {
      try {
        if (matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches || scrollY > 60 || sessionStorage.getItem('kv-shell')) return;
        sessionStorage.setItem('kv-shell', '1');
      } catch (e) { return; }
      s.classList.add('is-intro');
      var t0 = Date.now(), opened = false;
      function open() {
        if (opened) return; opened = true;
        var v = s.querySelector('.hero-veil'), p = s.querySelector('.hero-veil .c-pearl');
        if (v && p) {
          var a = v.getBoundingClientRect(), b = p.getBoundingClientRect();
          v.style.setProperty('--ix', Math.round(b.left + b.width / 2 - a.left) + 'px');
          v.style.setProperty('--iy', Math.round(b.top + b.height / 2 - a.top) + 'px');
        }
        s.classList.add('is-open');
        setTimeout(function () { s.classList.remove('is-intro', 'is-open'); }, 1500);
      }
      function go() { setTimeout(open, Math.max(0, 2850 - (Date.now() - t0))); }
      function ready() {
        var img = s.querySelector('.hero-media img');
        if (img && img.decode) img.decode().then(go, go); else go();
      }
      if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', ready); else ready();
      ['wheel', 'touchstart', 'keydown', 'pointerdown'].forEach(function (e) { addEventListener(e, open, { once: true, passive: true }); });
      setTimeout(open, 7000);
    })(document.currentScript.parentNode);
  </script>
  {%- elsif art or bloom -%}
  <script>
    (function (s) {
      try {
        if (matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches || scrollY > 60 || sessionStorage.getItem('kv-shell')) return;
        sessionStorage.setItem('kv-shell', '1');
      } catch (e) { return; }
      s.classList.add('is-drawing');
    })(document.currentScript.parentNode);
  </script>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if filmed -%}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      The films are theme files (assets/banner-film-desktop.mp4, 2560 x 1440; banner-film-phone.mp4,
      1440 x 2560), served as they are. Settings > Files re-encodes every film to at most 1080 on its
      longer side, which cut the upright phone film to 606 x 1080 (owner: "the video quality on mobile
      is not great", 2026-11-19). The two video settings stay as a way back.

      Phones play the original film itself (owner, 2026-11-22: "use the original 4k video for mobile
      version first page, do not change anything at all"): the iPhone's own file, 2160 x 3840 HEVC HDR,
      60 fps, 26.7 MB, with its own words in it, byte for byte as filmed. It is too big for a theme file
      (20 MB), so it is in Settings > Files (karineko-film-original-4k.mov), which keeps every upload's
      original beside the copies it makes, at the address on the line under this comment.

      Since 2026-11-23 (owner: "use everything from the 4k video and add no text to the film") laptops play
      it too, shown as the same band as their poster (rows 1400 to 2615), and a browser that can't play it
      smoothly (no HEVC, or not 4K at 60; or it hasn't arrived within 20 s) gets the 1440 films made from it,
      its own words in them (banner-film-desktop.mp4 is that band, banner-film-phone.mp4 the whole frame).
      The last frames shown with reduced motion are the original's too, words and all.

      Since 2026-11-23 (owner: "think about how you can trim the video to keep it under 20mb", then "Yes,
      switch it") the 4K film is a theme file, banner-film-4k.mp4: the original re-encoded by Apple's own
      HEVC export (avconvert PresetHEVC3840x2160), the same 2160 x 3840, 60 fps, HDR (HLG with its Dolby
      Vision layer), sound and frames, 13.9 MB instead of 26.7 (PSNR 46.7 dB, SSIM 0.990 against the
      original: no difference to see), its index at the front so it starts sooner. The untouched original
      stays in Settings > Files, at that address, as a way back.
    endcomment
    assign src_d = 'banner-film-desktop.mp4' | asset_url
    assign src_p = 'banner-film-phone.mp4' | asset_url
    # The untouched original: https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/70759d863a6c4a729b32f156cbe5dec5.mov
    assign src_o = 'banner-film-4k.mp4' | asset_url
    assign film_title = section.settings.film_title | default: 'KARINEKO VINTAGE'
  -%}
  {%- comment -%} The film holds still for a while as the page starts to scroll (owner, 2026-11-20: "stop/stall
      before it gets down, so you feel you have to scroll harder"): it sticks inside .film-hold, a screen plus
      70% tall, then scrolls away with a clean edge. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="film-hold">
  <div class="film">
    <h1 class="vh">{{ film_title }}{% if section.settings.film_line != blank %}: {{ section.settings.film_line }}{% endif %}</h1>
    {%- comment -%} The first frame, a real image fetched first (the page's largest paint), small for phones. {%- endcomment -%}
    <picture class="film-poster">
      <source media="(max-width: 749px)" srcset="{{ 'banner-video-phone-first.jpg' | asset_url }}" width="1080" height="1920">
      <img src="{{ 'banner-video-desktop-first.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="1440" height="810" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
    </picture>
    <video class="film-video" muted playsinline preload="auto" aria-hidden="true" data-desktop="{{ src_d }}" data-phone="{{ src_p }}" data-original="{{ src_o }}"></video>
    {%- comment -%} The last frame: only fetched when shown (reduced motion, no JavaScript). {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="film-end" style="--last-d:url({{ 'banner-video-desktop-last.jpg' | asset_url }});--last-p:url({{ 'banner-video-phone-last.jpg' | asset_url }})"></div>
    {%- comment -%} A small cue at the film's foot that there is more below (owner, 2026-11-19); it fades once the page moves. {%- endcomment -%}
    <a class="film-cue" href="#after-film"><span class="film-cue-word">{{ 'home.scroll_cue' | t }}</span><svg class="film-cue-arrow" viewBox="0 0 34 18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 2l15 14L32 2"/></svg></a>
  </div>
  </div>
  <script>
    /* The film (owner, 2026-11-19): plays once and holds its last frame (it looped for an hour; "change
       back to play once"). It only starts loading once its first frame is on screen (on a slow phone it
       otherwise took the bandwidth). It stays edge to edge (the framed-card ease-back is gone, 2026-11-20).
       The original (owner, 2026-11-23: "use everything from the 4k video") where the browser plays 4K HEVC
       smoothly: fetched whole before it plays, so it never stops to load half-way, with its poster (the
       same first frame) showing meanwhile; if it hasn't come within 20 s, or won't play, the 1440 film. */
    (function (f) {
      var v = f.querySelector('.film-video'), still = true;
      try { still = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches; } catch (e) {}
      var phone = matchMedia('(max-width: 749px)').matches;
      var src = phone ? v.getAttribute('data-phone') : v.getAttribute('data-desktop'), o = v.getAttribute('data-original');
      if (still || !src) { f.classList.add('is-still'); return; }
      var img = f.querySelector('.film-poster img'), started = false, own = false;
      function play(s) {
        v.src = s; v.classList.add('is-in');
        var p = v.play();
        if (p && p.catch) p.catch(function (e) {
          var n = e && e.name;
          if (n === 'AbortError' || (own && n === 'NotSupportedError')) return;   /* a new source took over, or will (see 'error') */
          own = false; f.classList.remove('is-own'); f.classList.add('is-still');   /* not allowed to play: its last frame */
        });
      }
      function fallback() { if (!own) return; own = false; f.classList.remove('is-own'); play(src); }
      function smooth(done) {
        var type = 'video/mp4; codecs="hvc1.2.4.L153.B0"', mc = navigator.mediaCapabilities;
        if (!o || !window.fetch || !window.URL || !v.canPlayType(type)) return done(false);
        if (!mc || !mc.decodingInfo) return done(true);
        mc.decodingInfo({ type: 'file', video: { contentType: type, width: 2160, height: 3840, bitrate: 39448742, framerate: 60 } })
          .then(function (d) { done(!!(d.supported && d.smooth)); }, function () { done(true); });
      }
      function go() {
        if (started) return; started = true;
        smooth(function (yes) {
          if (!yes) return play(src);
          own = true; f.classList.add('is-own');
          var ctl = window.AbortController ? new AbortController() : null, late = false;
          var t = setTimeout(function () { late = true; if (ctl) ctl.abort(); fallback(); }, 20000);
          fetch(o, ctl ? { signal: ctl.signal } : {}).then(function (r) { if (!r.ok) throw r.status; return r.blob(); }).then(function (b) {
            clearTimeout(t);
            if (!late && own) play(URL.createObjectURL(b));
          }).catch(function () { clearTimeout(t); fallback(); });
        });
      }
      v.addEventListener('error', fallback);
      if (img && !(img.complete && img.naturalWidth)) { img.addEventListener('load', go); img.addEventListener('error', go); setTimeout(go, 6000); }
      else go();
    })(document.currentScript.previousElementSibling.querySelector('.film'));
  </script>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if section.settings.backdrop == 'bloom' -%}
  <div class="hero-bloom" aria-hidden="true">
    <picture>
      <source media="(max-width: 749px)" sizes="100vw"
        srcset="{{ 'banner-bloom-phone-750.jpg' | asset_url }} 750w, {{ 'banner-bloom-phone-1100.jpg' | asset_url }} 1100w">
      <img src="{{ 'banner-bloom-1700.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="2752" height="1536" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
        srcset="{{ 'banner-bloom-1200.jpg' | asset_url }} 1200w, {{ 'banner-bloom-1700.jpg' | asset_url }} 1700w, {{ 'banner-bloom-2200.jpg' | asset_url }} 2200w" sizes="100vw">
    </picture>
    <span class="hero-leaves" style="--leaves:url({{ 'banner-leaves.jpg' | asset_url }})"></span>
    <span class="hero-glow"></span>
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if split -%}<div class="shell hero-split">{%- endif -%}
  {%- if art -%}
  <div class="hero-art">{%- render 'conch', place: 'banner' -%}</div>
  {%- elsif bloom or filmed -%}
    {%- comment -%} The flowers or the film are the picture: no photograph, no placeholder. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- else -%}
  <div class="hero-media hero-media--{{ fit }}{% if img_m %} has-mobile{% endif %}{% unless img %} is-empty{% endunless %}">
    {%- if img and split -%}
      {%- assign split_img = img_m | default: img -%}
      {%- assign alt_text = section.settings.image_alt | default: split_img.alt -%}
      {{ split_img | image_url: width: 1800 | image_tag: widths: '600, 900, 1200, 1500, 1800', sizes: '(max-width: 899px) 100vw, 58vw',
          loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', alt: alt_text }}
    {%- elsif img -%}
      <picture>
        {%- if img_m -%}
          <source media="(max-width: 749px)"
            srcset="{{ img_m | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w, {{ img_m | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ img_m | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w, {{ img_m | image_url: width: 1250 }} 1250w, {{ img_m | image_url: width: 1500 }} 1500w"
            sizes="100vw">
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign focal = img.presentation.focal_point | default: '50% 50%'
          assign obj_style = 'object-position: ' | append: focal
          assign alt_text = section.settings.image_alt | default: img.alt
        -%}
        {{ img | image_url: width: 3000 | image_tag:
            widths: '750, 1100, 1500, 2000, 2600, 3000', sizes: '100vw',
            loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', alt: alt_text, style: obj_style }}
      </picture>
    {%- else -%}
      <canvas data-seed="3" data-tone="light" data-comp="none" data-ratio="{{ ratio }}" data-fill="1"
              role="img" aria-label="{{ 'home.brand_image_to_follow' | t }}"></canvas>
      {%- if request.design_mode -%}
        <span class="stamp">Brand image · choose it in this section's settings</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if section.settings.shell == 'picture' -%}{%- render 'conch', place: 'picture' -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if section.settings.shell == 'intro' -%}<div class="hero-veil" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'conch', place: 'intro' -%}</div>{%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="{% unless split %}shell {% endunless %}hero-txt"{% if filmed %} id="after-film"{% endif %}>
    {%- unless filmed -%}
    <div class="hero-lead">
      {%- if section.settings.shell == 'above' -%}{%- render 'conch', place: 'above' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}<p class="eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.logo and line == false -%}
        <h1 class="hero-logo">{%- render 'lockup', height: 'clamp(96px, 17vw, 168px)' -%}</h1>
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}<p class="hero-h">{{ section.settings.heading }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <h1 class="hero-h">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    {%- endunless -%}
    {%- unless line -%}
    <div class="hero-side">
      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}<div class="hero-b">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        {%- if section.settings.show_link and section.settings.link_label != blank and section.settings.link != blank -%}
          <a class="{% if split %}btn btn--inline{% else %}hero-link{% endif %}" href="{{ section.settings.link }}">{{ section.settings.link_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.link2_label != blank and link2 != blank -%}
          <a class="hero-link" href="{{ link2 }}">{{ section.settings.link2_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endunless -%}
  </div>
  {%- if split -%}</div>{%- endif -%}
</section>
{% schema %}
{ "name": "Brand image",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image",
      "info": "Landscape, at least 2400px wide. Set the focal point on the image so phone crops keep the subject." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image_mobile", "label": "Phone image (optional)",
      "info": "Portrait. Used under 750px wide instead of cropping the image above." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Image description",
      "info": "Read aloud by screen readers. Describe the picture, not the brand." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "height", "label": "Shape on desktop", "default": "standard",
      "options": [
        { "value": "wide", "label": "Wide, 21:9" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "Standard, 16:9" },
        { "value": "tall", "label": "Tall, 4:3" },
        { "value": "adapt", "label": "As the image" }
      ] },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "one_line", "label": "Just the heading, on one line", "default": false,
      "info": "No logo, text or links under the picture, in every language." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "logo", "label": "Logo as the heading", "default": true,
      "info": "The shop's logo in large, with the heading as the line under it." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading",
      "default": "We make vintage luxury accessible" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Text",
      "default": "<p>Handpicked vintage pieces from Japan.</p><p>100% Authenticity Guaranteed.</p><p>London showings by appointment only.</p>" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "heading_face", "label": "Heading typeface", "default": "theme",
      "options": [ { "value": "theme", "label": "The site's serif" }, { "value": "hand", "label": "Handwriting" }, { "value": "aboreto", "label": "Aboreto (capitals)" } ],
      "info": "English and Spanish pages. Chinese, Japanese and Arabic keep the site's faces." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "text_face", "label": "Text typeface", "default": "theme",
      "options": [ { "value": "theme", "label": "The site's sans" }, { "value": "aboreto", "label": "Aboreto (capitals)" }, { "value": "hand", "label": "Handwriting" } ] },
    { "type": "select", "id": "shell", "label": "Shell drawing", "default": "none",
      "options": [ { "value": "none", "label": "None" }, { "value": "banner", "label": "Large, instead of the picture" }, { "value": "intro", "label": "Large, opening the picture" }, { "value": "above", "label": "Small, above the heading" }, { "value": "picture", "label": "Small, on the picture" } ],
      "info": "A spiral shell with a pearl that draws itself as the page opens. Instead of the picture: no photograph, the shell above the words. Opening the picture: it draws on a veil over the picture, which then opens from the pearl, once per visit." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "backdrop", "label": "Background", "default": "none",
      "options": [ { "value": "none", "label": "The page colour" }, { "value": "bloom", "label": "Pale flowers on linen, with moving light" }, { "value": "film", "label": "The film, then the words on its last frame" } ],
